    "updated_at": "2018-05-22T08:06:34Z",
    "body": "Thank you, @domenic! Of course I was talking about the setSelectionRange(), sorry for that (the example I have shared is using it correctly). I was thinking the same - that browsers needs to handle this but I wanted to be sure about that. You can see that in this [discussion](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=806233) the guys from Google asked me to log it as an issue is [w3c ](https://github.com/w3c/editing/issues/173) and then I was redirected to you.\r\n\r\nIt seems that [Microsoft ](https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/platform/issues/15637833/) have already implemented it and the text is scrolled and caret is visible and I believe this is the expected behavior. As you said, it seems that each browsers decides how to implement it, but anyway for me it seems that still this is something Chrome needs to fix. I will give them your answer and will see what they think and if they have a reasonable explanation why not to implement it in a way so that text is scrolled and caret is visible. Thank you!",
